        "jurisdiction:ca-on"
      ],
      "quickAnswer": "The ruffed grouse (Bonasa umbellus) is a resident forest grouse found widely across Canada's deciduous and mixed-wood forests. It is strongly associated with structurally varied forest, especially young and regenerating hardwood cover near older stands. Hunting legality depends on the jurisdiction, management unit, date, licence and current official rules.",
